course: dictionary
lesson: 7613
title: Many meanings: private
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Private has more than one meaning, so context tells you which one to use. Ask yourself what the word is describing. Is it about a person, a place, a school, or a soldier?
explain: «Keep your password private» means keep it secret and do not share it with others. «The head teacher has a private room» means the room is only for one person, not for everyone.
explain: «The town has a private school, not run by the government» uses the meaning not run by the government. «A private stood guard at the gate» uses the noun, a soldier of the lowest rank. Check the clues, then try your meaning in the sentence.
fact: Private means belonging to or for one person or group only, not for everyone.
fact: Private means secret or personal, not to be shared with others.
fact: Private means not run by the government, as in a private school.
fact: A private is a soldier of the lowest rank.
fact: «Private property» means do not enter.
exercise: «Keep your password private.» What does private mean here? | Belonging to the government | Very loud | Open to everyone | *Secret, not to be shared with others
exercise: The sign said «Private property». What does it tell you? | The land is for sale | *Do not enter | Please come in and look around | There is a shop inside
exercise: «A private stood guard at the gate.» In this sentence, what is a private? | A secret | A room for one person | A school run by the government | *A soldier of the lowest rank
test: Which of these is private information that should not be shared with strangers? | The weather today | The name of a bird | *Your home address | The word for a river
test: «Josiah wanted to talk in private.» What does in private mean? | Being sold in a shop | At the top of a hill | In a loud room full of people | *With nobody else there
exam: «Dad said his work problems are private, so I will not repeat them.» What does private mean? | A loud noise | *Secret and personal, not to be passed on | A soldier's rank | Given to everyone at school
